For example, Fig. 1a, the metapath {Target — (member of) → PPI (PPI network) ← (member of) — Protein — (associated with) → Disease} summarizes multiple meta paths for PPI data. The PPI data are aggregated from the STRING database (STRINGDb)46, and the corresponding SQL is: SELECT protein1_id, protein2_id, score AS combined_score FROM ppi WHERE ppitype = ’STRINGDB’. Such an example would be {IL1B — (member of) → KEGG Alzheimer’s Disease pathway ← (member of) — MAPT — (associated with) → MAPK signaling pathway}. Type-specific metapath counts can be combined using Degree Weighted Path Counts (DWPCs, Eq. 1)\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
